---
import SimLayout from '../../../layouts/SimLayout.astro';
---

<SimLayout
  areaSlug="deep-learning"
  title="Embeddings & Cosine Similarity"
  description="An embedding turns a word into an arrow. Two words mean similar things when their arrows point the same way, so similarity is an angle and nothing else. Or is it? Rank the same words by straight-line distance instead and the level sets change from rays out of the origin into rings around the query, which is a different question with different answers, unless every arrow has length one."
>
  <div class="sim">
    <div class="sim-stage">
      <canvas id="cos" width="820" height="510"></canvas>
    </div>

    <div class="sim-panel">
      <div class="control">
        <label>Rank the words by</label>
        <div class="seg" id="score">
          <button data-s="cos" class="active">cos θ</button>
          <button data-s="dot">dot product</button>
          <button data-s="euc">distance</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label for="compare">Compare the query with</label>
        <select id="compare">
          <option value="best">its best match</option>
        </select>
      </div>

      <div class="wlist" id="list"></div>

      <label class="check"
        ><input type="checkbox" id="unit" /> Force the query to length 1</label
      >
      <label class="check"
        ><input type="checkbox" id="proj" checked />
        <span id="projlbl">Show the shadow the query casts</span></label
      >

      <div class="readout">
        <div class="row"><span>Angle θ</span><b id="ang">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>cos θ</span><b id="cosv">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Dot product</span><b id="dotv">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Distance ‖q−w‖</span><b id="eucv">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span>Query length</span><b id="qlen">—</b></div>
      </div>

      <p class="note">
        Drag the arrow anywhere on the stage to move the query, or click a word to
        compare with it. Real embeddings have hundreds of dimensions; this one has
        two so the angle is something you can see.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="observe">
    <li>
      Swing the query around the circle. The match changes the moment the
      <b>angle</b> changes, and it never changes while you only make the arrow
      longer or shorter. Cosine similarity divides the length out, so it measures
      <b>direction alone</b>.
    </li>
    <li>
      cos θ runs from <b>1</b> (same direction, same meaning) through <b>0</b> (at
      right angles, unrelated) to <b>−1</b> (opposite). Lay the query straight on
      <b>puppy</b> and the panel reads 1.00, with dog just behind it, car near 0
      and king below zero. Those numbers are the whole of semantic search.
    </li>
    <li>
      Turn on the shadow. The dashed line drops the query tip onto the word's
      direction, and the bright segment left behind has length |q| cos θ. That
      shadow is what the dot product measures; the cosine is the same shadow after
      dividing by both lengths.
    </li>
    <li>
      Now switch the ranking to <b>dot product</b>. The generic word <b>thing</b>,
      drawn long because it appears everywhere, takes over the top spot from
      whatever you are actually pointing at. Raw dot products reward long vectors,
      which is exactly why retrieval systems normalise and use the cosine.
    </li>
    <li>
      Tick <b>force the query to length 1</b>. Every arrow now sits on the circle,
      the dot product and the cosine become the same number, and the shadow is
      literally cos θ. Normalised embeddings are used precisely so these two agree.
    </li>
    <li>
      Switch the ranking to <b>distance</b>. The picture changes shape: the
      cosine's level sets are <b>rays out of the origin</b>, so length is
      invisible to it, while distance measures rings <b>around the query tip</b>,
      so a word can lose simply by being long. Watch <b>kitten</b>, a short arrow,
      beat <b>cat</b> whenever your query is short, even though cat points more
      the way you are pointing.
    </li>
    <li>
      Then put both on the circle: tick <b>length 1</b> and click a word whose
      arrow is already about that long. Now the two rankings agree, always, and
      they must, because ‖q−w‖² = 2 − 2 cos θ when both have length one. That one
      identity is why a vector database can index cosine similarity with a
      nearest-neighbour structure that only knows how to measure distance.
    </li>
  </Fragment>
</SimLayout>

<script>
  import { setupCanvas, makeText } from '../../../lib/sim';

  const canvas = document.getElementById('cos') as HTMLCanvasElement;
  const { ctx, W, H } = setupCanvas(canvas, () => draw());
  const css = (v: string, f = '') =>
    getComputedStyle(canvas).getPropertyValue(v).trim() || f;
  const ink = (a: number) => `rgba(${css('--stage-ink', '232,233,236')},${a})`;
  const { label } = makeText(ctx, ink);
  const accent = () => css('--accent', '#7c8cff');
  const teal = () => css('--accent-2', '#5eead4');

  // A hand-made two-dimensional "embedding": words that mean similar things
  // point the same way, and `thing` is long the way a very frequent generic
  // word is long in a real model.
  const WORDS = [
    { w: 'king', a: 76, r: 0.84 },
    { w: 'queen', a: 102, r: 0.79 },
    { w: 'cat', a: 162, r: 0.92 },
    { w: 'kitten', a: 180, r: 0.58 },
    { w: 'dog', a: 204, r: 0.96 },
    { w: 'puppy', a: 224, r: 0.62 },
    { w: 'thing', a: 244, r: 1.42 },
    { w: 'car', a: 316, r: 0.88 },
    { w: 'truck', a: 334, r: 0.74 },
  ];

  const state = {
    qa: (232 * Math.PI) / 180,
    ql: 0.8,
    score: 'cos' as 'cos' | 'dot' | 'euc',
    compare: 'best',
    unit: false,
    proj: true,
  };

  const C = { x: 300, y: 238, R: 158 };
  const rad = (deg: number) => (deg * Math.PI) / 180;
  const toX = (a: number, r: number) => C.x + C.R * r * Math.cos(a);
  const toY = (a: number, r: number) => C.y - C.R * r * Math.sin(a);
  const qlen = () => (state.unit ? 1 : state.ql);

  const cosOf = (a: number) => Math.cos(a - state.qa);
  const dotOf = (a: number, r: number) => qlen() * r * Math.cos(a - state.qa);
  /** ‖q − w‖, straight-line distance between the two arrow tips. */
  const eucOf = (a: number, r: number) =>
    Math.sqrt(
      Math.max(0, qlen() ** 2 + r * r - 2 * qlen() * r * Math.cos(a - state.qa))
    );
  /** What a word is ranked by. Always bigger = better, so distance is negated. */
  const scoreOf = (word: { a: number; r: number }) =>
    state.score === 'cos'
      ? cosOf(rad(word.a))
      : state.score === 'dot'
        ? dotOf(rad(word.a), word.r)
        : -eucOf(rad(word.a), word.r);
  /** What the ranking prints: a distance is shown as the positive number it is. */
  const shownOf = (word: { a: number; r: number }) =>
    state.score === 'euc' ? eucOf(rad(word.a), word.r) : scoreOf(word);

  function ranked() {
    return WORDS.map((x) => ({ ...x, s: scoreOf(x) })).sort((p, q) => q.s - p.s);
  }
  function target() {
    if (state.compare !== 'best') {
      const f = WORDS.find((x) => x.w === state.compare);
      if (f) return f;
    }
    return ranked()[0];
  }

  function arrow(a: number, r: number, colour: string, width: number) {
    const x = toX(a, r),
      y = toY(a, r);
    ctx.strokeStyle = colour;
    ctx.lineWidth = width;
    ctx.lineCap = 'round';
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(C.x, C.y);
    ctx.lineTo(x, y);
    ctx.stroke();
    const head = 5 + width * 1.8;
    ctx.fillStyle = colour;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x, y);
    ctx.lineTo(
      x - head * Math.cos(a - 0.38),
      y + head * Math.sin(a - 0.38)
    );
    ctx.lineTo(
      x - head * Math.cos(a + 0.38),
      y + head * Math.sin(a + 0.38)
    );
    ctx.closePath();
    ctx.fill();
  }

  function draw() {
    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
    const t = target();
    const ta = rad(t.a);
    const q = state.qa;
    const c = cosOf(ta);
    const theta = (Math.acos(Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, c))) * 180) / Math.PI;

    // unit circle
    ctx.strokeStyle = ink(0.16);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.setLineDash([3, 5]);
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(C.x, C.y, C.R, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.setLineDash([]);
    label('length 1', C.x + C.R + 8, C.y - 6, 0.3, 'left', 10.5);

    const dist = eucOf(ta, t.r);

    // the shadow of the query on the matched direction
    if (state.proj && state.score !== 'euc') {
      const shadow = qlen() * c;
      ctx.strokeStyle = ink(0.14);
      ctx.lineWidth = 1;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(toX(ta, -1.5), toY(ta, -1.5));
      ctx.lineTo(toX(ta, 1.7), toY(ta, 1.7));
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.strokeStyle = teal();
      ctx.lineWidth = 6;
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.35;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(C.x, C.y);
      ctx.lineTo(toX(ta, shadow), toY(ta, shadow));
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
      ctx.strokeStyle = ink(0.35);
      ctx.setLineDash([4, 4]);
      ctx.lineWidth = 1;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(toX(q, qlen()), toY(q, qlen()));
      ctx.lineTo(toX(ta, shadow), toY(ta, shadow));
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.setLineDash([]);
    }

    // Distance mode draws what it actually measures: the straight line between
    // the two tips, and the ring of everything else exactly that far from the
    // query. The cosine's level sets are rays out of the origin; these are not.
    if (state.score === 'euc') {
      const qxp = toX(q, qlen()),
        qyp = toY(q, qlen());
      ctx.save();
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.rect(0, 0, 552, H);
      ctx.clip();
      if (state.proj) {
        ctx.strokeStyle = ink(0.12);
        ctx.setLineDash([2, 5]);
        ctx.lineWidth = 1;
        for (const rr of [0.35, 0.7, 1.05, 1.4]) {
          ctx.beginPath();
          ctx.arc(qxp, qyp, C.R * rr, 0, Math.PI * 2);
          ctx.stroke();
        }
        ctx.setLineDash([]);
      }
      ctx.strokeStyle = `${teal()}66`;
      ctx.lineWidth = 1.5;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(qxp, qyp, C.R * dist, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.restore();

      ctx.strokeStyle = teal();
      ctx.lineWidth = 3;
      ctx.setLineDash([6, 4]);
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(qxp, qyp);
      ctx.lineTo(toX(ta, t.r), toY(ta, t.r));
      ctx.stroke();
      ctx.setLineDash([]);
      label(
        dist.toFixed(2),
        (qxp + toX(ta, t.r)) / 2,
        (qyp + toY(ta, t.r)) / 2 - 8,
        1,
        'center',
        11.5,
        teal()
      );
    }

    // angle wedge between the query and the compared word
    const wr = 74;
    let a0 = q,
      a1 = ta;
    if (((a1 - a0 + Math.PI * 4) % (Math.PI * 2)) > Math.PI) [a0, a1] = [a1, a0];
    if (state.score !== 'euc') {
      ctx.fillStyle = `${teal()}22`;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.moveTo(C.x, C.y);
      ctx.arc(C.x, C.y, wr, -a0, -a1, true);
      ctx.closePath();
      ctx.fill();
    }

    // the vocabulary
    for (const word of WORDS) {
      const a = rad(word.a);
      const on = word.w === t.w;
      arrow(a, word.r, on ? teal() : ink(0.3), on ? 3 : 1.6);
      const lx = toX(a, word.r) + 14 * Math.cos(a);
      const ly = toY(a, word.r) - 14 * Math.sin(a) + 4;
      label(
        word.w,
        lx,
        ly,
        on ? 1 : 0.5,
        Math.cos(a) < -0.25 ? 'right' : Math.cos(a) > 0.25 ? 'left' : 'center',
        on ? 13 : 12,
        on ? teal() : undefined
      );
    }

    // the query
    arrow(q, qlen(), accent(), 3.4);
    ctx.fillStyle = accent();
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(toX(q, qlen()), toY(q, qlen()), 7, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.fill();
    label(
      'query',
      toX(q, qlen()) + 26 * Math.cos(q),
      toY(q, qlen()) - 26 * Math.sin(q) + 4,
      1,
      Math.cos(q) < -0.25 ? 'right' : Math.cos(q) > 0.25 ? 'left' : 'center',
      12,
      accent()
    );

    // the answer, in words
    const bx = 590;
    const euc = state.score === 'euc';
    label(euc ? 'DISTANCE TO' : 'SIMILARITY WITH', bx, 176, 0.45, 'left', 11);
    label(t.w, bx, 214, 1, 'left', 22, teal());
    label(euc ? '‖q − w‖' : 'cos θ', bx, 268, 0.45, 'left', 11);
    label((euc ? dist : c).toFixed(2), bx, 312, 1, 'left', 30, accent());
    label(`θ = ${theta.toFixed(1)}°`, bx, 344, 0.55, 'left', 12);
    label(
      euc
        ? `‖q−w‖² = ${qlen().toFixed(2)}² + ${t.r.toFixed(2)}² − 2·${qlen().toFixed(2)}·${t.r.toFixed(2)}·cos θ`
        : state.proj
          ? `shadow = |q| cos θ = ${(qlen() * c).toFixed(2)}`
          : '',
      bx,
      370,
      0.45,
      'left',
      euc ? 9.5 : 11
    );
    if (euc && Math.abs(qlen() - t.r) < 0.06)
      label(
        'both about the same length, so this is 2 − 2 cos θ',
        bx,
        390,
        0.4,
        'left',
        9.5,
        teal()
      );
    label('drag the arrow · click a word', 32, 32, 0.32, 'left', 10.5);

    updatePanel(c, theta, t);
  }

  // --- panel -----------------------------------------------------------------
  const listEl = document.getElementById('list') as HTMLElement;
  const $ = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id) as HTMLElement;

  function updatePanel(c: number, theta: number, t: { w: string; r: number }) {
    const rows = ranked();
    const euc = state.score === 'euc';
    // A similarity is signed and grows from the middle; a distance is positive
    // and *smaller* is better, so its bar grows from the left as it shrinks.
    const span = Math.max(...rows.map((r) => Math.abs(r.s)), 0.001);
    listEl.innerHTML = rows
      .map((r) => {
        const shown = shownOf(r);
        const w = euc
          ? (1 - Math.abs(r.s) / span) * 100
          : (Math.abs(r.s) / span) * 50;
        const side = euc ? 'left:0' : r.s >= 0 ? 'left:50%' : 'right:50%';
        return `<div class="cs-row${euc ? ' full' : ''}${
          r.w === t.w ? ' sel' : ''
        }" data-w="${r.w}">
          <span class="nm">${r.w}</span>
          <span class="bar"><i style="${side};width:${w}%"></i><s></s></span>
          <b>${shown.toFixed(2)}</b>
        </div>`;
      })
      .join('');
    $('ang').textContent = `${theta.toFixed(1)}°`;
    $('cosv').textContent = c.toFixed(3);
    $('dotv').textContent = (qlen() * t.r * c).toFixed(3);
    $('eucv').textContent = eucOf(rad(WORDS.find((x) => x.w === t.w)!.a), t.r).toFixed(3);
    $('qlen').textContent = qlen().toFixed(2);
    $('projlbl').textContent = euc
      ? 'Show rings of equal distance'
      : 'Show the shadow the query casts';
  }

  const sel = $('compare') as HTMLSelectElement;
  for (const word of WORDS) {
    const o = document.createElement('option');
    o.value = word.w;
    o.textContent = word.w;
    sel.appendChild(o);
  }

  sel.addEventListener('change', () => {
    state.compare = sel.value;
    draw();
  });
  listEl.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const row = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('.cs-row') as HTMLElement | null;
    if (!row) return;
    state.compare = state.compare === row.dataset.w ? 'best' : row.dataset.w!;
    sel.value = state.compare;
    draw();
  });
  $('score').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const b = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button');
    if (!b) return;
    document
      .querySelectorAll('#score button')
      .forEach((x) => x.classList.remove('active'));
    b.classList.add('active');
    state.score = b.dataset.s as 'cos' | 'dot' | 'euc';
    draw();
  });
  ($('unit') as HTMLInputElement).addEventListener('change', (e) => {
    state.unit = (e.target as HTMLInputElement).checked;
    draw();
  });
  ($('proj') as HTMLInputElement).addEventListener('change', (e) => {
    state.proj = (e.target as HTMLInputElement).checked;
    draw();
  });

  // --- dragging --------------------------------------------------------------
  let dragging = false;
  function pointer(e: PointerEvent) {
    const b = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
    return {
      x: ((e.clientX - b.left) / b.width) * W,
      y: ((e.clientY - b.top) / b.height) * H,
    };
  }
  function setQuery(p: { x: number; y: number }) {
    const dx = p.x - C.x,
      dy = C.y - p.y;
    state.qa = Math.atan2(dy, dx);
    if (!state.unit)
      state.ql = Math.max(0.15, Math.min(1.6, Math.hypot(dx, dy) / C.R));
    draw();
  }

  canvas.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => {
    const p = pointer(e);
    // a click on a word tip pins the comparison instead of moving the query
    for (const word of WORDS) {
      const a = rad(word.a);
      if (Math.hypot(p.x - toX(a, word.r), p.y - toY(a, word.r)) < 22) {
        state.compare = state.compare === word.w ? 'best' : word.w;
        sel.value = state.compare;
        draw();
        return;
      }
    }
    dragging = true;
    canvas.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);
    setQuery(p);
  });
  canvas.addEventListener('pointermove', (e) => {
    if (dragging) setQuery(pointer(e));
  });
  canvas.addEventListener('pointerup', () => (dragging = false));
  canvas.addEventListener('pointercancel', () => (dragging = false));

  draw();
</script>

<style>
  #cos {
    cursor: crosshair;
    touch-action: none;
  }
  .sim-panel select {
    width: 100%;
    padding: 7px 9px;
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text);
    background: var(--bg-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }
  .wlist {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2px;
  }
  .check {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .note {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
</style>

<!-- The ranking rows are injected via innerHTML, so they never carry Astro's
     scoped attribute; these rules have to be global to reach them. -->
<style is:global>
  .cs-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 58px 1fr 40px;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 9px;
    padding: 4px 5px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .cs-row:hover {
    background: var(--bg-elev);
  }
  .cs-row.sel {
    background: var(--accent-soft);
  }
  .cs-row .nm {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .cs-row.sel .nm {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .cs-row .bar {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    height: 8px;
    background: var(--bg-elev);
    border-radius: 4px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .cs-row .bar i {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    background: var(--accent);
    opacity: 0.55;
  }
  .cs-row.sel .bar i {
    background: var(--accent-2);
    opacity: 0.9;
  }
  .cs-row.full .bar s {
    display: none;
  }
  .cs-row .bar s {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    width: 1px;
    background: var(--border-strong);
  }
  .cs-row b {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    text-align: right;
    color: var(--accent-2);
  }
</style>
